474
00:35:31,621 --> 00:35:36,580
will likely reinvigorate a reliable but controversial energy source,

475
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:38,500
nuclear fission power.

476
00:35:39,980 --> 00:35:43,260
My view is that we will see a wholesale shift

477
00:35:43,261 --> 00:35:45,240
in the public attitude toward nuclear power

478
00:35:45,241 --> 00:35:46,760
because the alternative is coal.

479
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:49,760
And so what we will see is a dramatic increase

480
00:35:49,761 --> 00:35:51,840
in the number of nuclear power plants around the world.

481
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:55,280
Scientists continue to chase the dream of nuclear fusion,

482
00:35:55,700 --> 00:35:57,400
both hot and cold.

483
00:35:58,720 --> 00:36:00,440
If it can be made practical,

484
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:03,700
fusion could be a limitless clean source of energy

485
00:36:03,701 --> 00:36:05,780
that very well may save us.

486
00:36:06,740 --> 00:36:10,040
Just one of the many ironies of the ultimate doomsday technology,

487
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:11,580
the atom.

488
00:36:13,640 --> 00:36:15,680
Cold fusion, once largely discredited,

489
00:36:16,300 --> 00:36:17,620
has gained renewed interest.

490
00:36:17,621 --> 00:36:21,340
In these cold fusion experiments at SRI International,

491
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:25,200
a low-energy laser irradiates a rod of palladium

492
00:36:25,201 --> 00:36:28,400
immersed in an electrolyte of deuterium-heavy water.

493
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:31,480
The reaction generates helium,

494
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:34,840
releasing 30 times the amount of the energy put in.

495
00:36:35,780 --> 00:36:38,640
In other words, evidence of a net energy gain,

496
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:40,740
fusion at room temperature.

497
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:45,380
The most powerful reason to look at fusion of any sort

498
00:36:45,381 --> 00:36:53,520
is that the deuterium, which is the fuel for fusion processes, can be obtained from seawater.

499
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:57,180
There is, in fact, enough deuterium in every gallon of seawater

500
00:36:57,181 --> 00:37:01,500
so that if converted to energy by a fusion process,

501
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:09,200
a gallon of seawater in its natural state has 30 times the energy density of a gallon of gasoline.

502
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:13,080
Whatever path we take, replacing our current energy regime

503
00:37:13,081 --> 00:37:16,540
will be one of the biggest jobs we've undertaken as a civilization.

504
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:25,560
In the 21st century, big jobs require small technology, like nanotechnology.

505
00:37:26,300 --> 00:37:29,580
But as nanotech converges with robotics, some say,

506
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:32,000
beware the doomsday nanobots.

507
00:37:34,740 --> 00:37:38,800
The Earth's surface receives more energy from the sun in one hour

508
00:37:38,801 --> 00:37:42,040
than all of humanity uses in one year.

509
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:47,960
Doomsday Tech will return on Modern Marvels, here on the History Channel.

510
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:57,940
Supercomputers, robots, cyborgs, androids.

511
00:37:58,500 --> 00:38:06,080
These intelligent machines, fictional or real, have long caused a vague uneasiness in the minds of the species who created them.

512
00:38:06,081 --> 00:38:12,960
A machine that turns against humans would be an especially cruel doomsday technology.

513
00:38:12,961 --> 00:38:18,780
Our fear of such a day may only increase as computers and robots become more human-like

514
00:38:18,781 --> 00:38:21,080
and human beings more machine-like.

515
00:38:21,081 --> 00:38:26,280
So we'll have very powerful non-biological systems that have the subtlety and suppleness

516
00:38:26,281 --> 00:38:31,180
and pattern recognition powers of human intelligence, combined with the ability to share knowledge

517
00:38:31,181 --> 00:38:35,160
instantly, to think much faster, much more accurately.

518
00:38:35,161 --> 00:38:42,600
But it's not just going to be a competitor, sort of an invasion of alien intelligence

519
00:38:42,601 --> 00:38:43,920
coming from over the horizon.

520
00:38:43,921 --> 00:38:47,760
It's emerging from within our civilization, and we're going to quite literally merge with

521
00:38:47,761 --> 00:38:50,080
this technology.

522
00:38:50,081 --> 00:38:55,640
The age-old fear that machines may one day get the better of man has surfaced again,

523
00:38:55,641 --> 00:39:00,200
this time due to the cutting-edge field known as nanotechnology.

524
00:39:00,201 --> 00:39:04,440
Nanotechnology is anything that is of nanometer scale.

525
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:10,020
That's 10 to the minus 9 meters, or about 1,000th the size of a human hair.

526
00:39:10,580 --> 00:39:13,960
Also called molecular manufacturing, or atom tech,

527
00:39:14,900 --> 00:39:18,620
nanotechnology is essentially manufacturing with tiny bits of matter,

528
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:20,680
even down to the atom.

529
00:39:21,680 --> 00:39:24,260
It can create new super-strong materials,

530
00:39:24,540 --> 00:39:29,880
and even tiny machines that will build more tiny machines on nano assembly lines.

531
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:37,200
The positive applications of nanotech are virtually limitless.

532
00:39:37,201 --> 00:39:44,200
The recent introduction of nanonichel may cut the cost of automotive fuel cells by 75%.

533
00:39:44,201 --> 00:39:50,200
New devices detect chemical warfare agents using parts assembled on the molecular level.

534
00:39:50,201 --> 00:39:54,200
Nanomedicine is especially intriguing.

535
00:39:54,201 --> 00:39:58,200
In the near term, there's some very exciting work taking a nanoparticle,

536
00:39:58,201 --> 00:40:04,200
coating half of it with gold, putting a functional molecule on the other end,

537
00:40:04,201 --> 00:40:11,200
sending it into a biological system such that this molecule here binds to a cancer,

538
00:40:11,201 --> 00:40:12,200
I believe in my lifetime.

539
00:40:12,201 --> 00:40:16,200
Very small nanosystems will be injected by a surgeon into the body

540
00:40:16,201 --> 00:40:21,200
to actually do repair of tissues, cells and molecules in the body.

541
00:40:21,201 --> 00:40:27,200
Any technology this powerful and this tiny must have a potential downside.

542
00:40:27,201 --> 00:40:30,820
and even nanotech proponents warn of potential abuses.

543
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:35,960
The main fear has to do with the future of nanomachines, or nanobots,

544
00:40:36,780 --> 00:40:39,420
specifically self-replicating nanobots.

545
00:40:41,300 --> 00:40:49,180
Self-replication will be needed constructively in order to scale up nanobots to a useful level,

546
00:40:49,300 --> 00:40:51,820
because one nanobot doesn't do anything. You need trillions of them.

547
00:40:51,900 --> 00:40:56,240
So at some level, there has to be self-replication to get up to those numbers.

548
00:40:56,241 --> 00:41:01,700
Critics ranging from Sun Microsystems founder Bill Joy to the Prince of Wales

549
00:41:01,701 --> 00:41:04,480
warn of a terrifying doomsday scenario.

550
00:41:04,481 --> 00:41:10,360
The year 2046.

551
00:41:10,361 --> 00:41:20,180
In a common practice, billions of nanobots designed to consume hydrocarbons are released

552
00:41:20,181 --> 00:41:23,120
to absorb an oil spill off the coast of Louisiana.

553
00:41:23,121 --> 00:41:25,120
But the nanobots, through a programming error,

554
00:41:25,121 --> 00:41:29,120
begin devouring all carbon-based life forms around them.

555
00:41:29,121 --> 00:41:32,120
As they self-replicate exponentially,

556
00:41:32,121 --> 00:41:35,120
they replace all matter with copies of themselves.

557
00:41:35,121 --> 00:41:38,120
Within days, the world is turned to dust.

558
00:41:39,120 --> 00:41:42,120
This scenario has been termed gray goo.

559
00:41:42,121 --> 00:41:45,120
It's the exact same specter we see in biology,

560
00:41:45,121 --> 00:41:49,120
where you have viruses or bacteria or cancer cells just replicate.

561
00:41:49,121 --> 00:41:51,120
I mean, cancer cells start replicating,

562
00:41:51,121 --> 00:41:54,720
replicating and then they take over our bodies and turn all of our good cells

563
00:41:54,721 --> 00:41:59,160
into copies of themselves and so uncontrolled self replication is a great

564
00:41:59,161 --> 00:42:04,620
danger this is at the moment still science fiction and many of us think it

565
00:42:04,621 --> 00:42:09,780
will remain so but of course we have to bear in mind that many things that seem

566
00:42:09,781 --> 00:42:15,720
science fiction a hundred years ago have become stark reality by now and so the

567
00:42:15,721 --> 00:42:25,280
The possibility that nanomachines may have unintended consequences is something which all those involved in that technology should be mindful of, in my opinion.

568
00:42:26,300 --> 00:42:35,320
This may be especially relevant if nanotechnology continues to merge with the human mind and body, which many experts in the field would like to promote.

569
00:42:36,700 --> 00:42:42,000
We're ultimately going to have a world where we're going to have billions, in fact trillions of nanobots.

570
00:42:42,001 --> 00:42:43,660
They'll be in our bodies keeping us healthy.

571
00:42:43,820 --> 00:42:46,020
They'll be in our environment keeping the environment healthy.

572
00:42:46,580 --> 00:42:48,380
And they're going to be running software.

573
00:42:48,860 --> 00:42:51,080
And it's really going to be a means of who controls that software.

574
00:42:51,760 --> 00:42:52,820
One thing is clear.

575
00:42:53,360 --> 00:42:56,420
In the 21st century, small will be big.

576
00:42:57,520 --> 00:43:00,740
Computer science, biology, genetics, and robotics

577
00:43:00,741 --> 00:43:03,520
are all beginning to converge on the nano level.

578
00:43:04,900 --> 00:43:08,420
It will take considerable effort to ensure that small technology

579
00:43:08,421 --> 00:43:10,220
doesn't become a big problem.

580
00:43:10,221 --> 00:43:14,620
I do believe that this is going to be the next industrial revolution.

581
00:43:14,820 --> 00:43:19,000
This is going to be a very, very big change for our species

582
00:43:19,001 --> 00:43:22,080
in terms of what we will be able to do,

583
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:26,420
both positively and potentially causing some problems.

584
00:43:27,380 --> 00:43:30,720
As with all technology, the cutting edge cuts both ways.

585
00:43:32,100 --> 00:43:34,860
The energy source that created the modern world

586
00:43:34,861 --> 00:43:36,700
